<p>Brazil’s Supreme Court has allowed former president Jair Bolsonaro to serve his 27-year prison sentence at home for an initial 90 days on medical grounds, after he was hospitalized on March 13 in Brasília with pneumonia or bronchopneumonia. The ruling changes where Bolsonaro will serve the sentence, not the conviction itself, which stems from an attempted coup after Brazil’s 2022 election.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/jT_b-MZI1sqoEybFJvqGvINGjyaS9zNPkz6HKsb_ubcVe04elREMBzPJXr93viGNSz_Sy67KPlfD2PnRiCdrVtLMAV7vxGMkHKNYDoJS5AVbtry9s7PAnkj363YDzwogl9hCvfrOhTTx8sbm0Z2wwds3ve3hSTTZM9hfoTmNYJzCIn_e1AMAVLzK-t7P6N60ME3cjHAO74ezBBE4AbXHiy9I6T04WF0YqpU1_5-tKKj7J5jbCTECVJuZoobgDSJKortrTRmISMQQt6-x1g' alt='Former Brazilian President Jair Bolsonaro after medical tests at DF Star hospital in Brasília on August 16, 2025; a Supreme Court judge later authorized him to serve his sentence under humanitarian house arrest once discharged from hospital.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Home-detention rules: The Hindu said Bolsonaro must wear an ankle monitor and cannot use cellphones while serving the sentence at home.</li><li>Custody before the move: Le Monde reported that he had been serving the sentence at Brasília’s Papuda penitentiary complex since mid-January.</li><li>Length of hospital stay: Several reports said he had spent 11 days in the hospital before the court allowed the move to home detention.</li><li>Age noted in coverage: Bolsonaro is 71.</li></ul><blockquote>I authorise temporary humanitarian house arrest … for an initial period of 90 days - Alexandre de Moraes</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Justice Alexandre de Moraes called the move &#x27;humanitarian house arrest&#x27; and said any extension beyond the first 90 days would depend on continued medical need. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3347769/judge-allows-brazils-bolsonaro-serve-27-year-sentence-home-due-ill-health'>South China Morning Post</a>, <a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/24/brazil-jair-bolsonaro-house-arrest-health'>The Guardian</a>, <a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/brazils-bolsonaro-to-serve-sentence-at-home-due-to-ill-health-judge-to-review-in-90-days/article70782446.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Implementation angle: The Hindu focused on how the order will work at Bolsonaro’s residence, with local police monitoring the gated-community home and protesters barred from gathering outside. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/brazils-bolsonaro-to-serve-sentence-at-home-due-to-ill-health-judge-to-review-in-90-days/article70782446.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-brazil-bolsonaro-prison-house-health/'>Former Brazilian president Bolsonaro to serve 27-year sentence at home due to poor health</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/bolsonaro-allowed-to-serve-27-year-sentence-at-home-due-to-ill-health'>Bolsonaro allowed to serve 27-year sentence at home due to ill health</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3347769/judge-allows-brazils-bolsonaro-serve-27-year-sentence-home-due-ill-health'>Brazil court grants house arrest for jailed Bolsonaro due to ill health</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/24/brazil-jair-bolsonaro-house-arrest-health'>Jailed Bolsonaro granted ‘humanitarian house arrest’ amid failing health</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/brazils-bolsonaro-to-serve-sentence-at-home-due-to-ill-health-judge-to-review-in-90-days/article70782446.ece'>Brazil&#x27;s Bolsonaro to serve sentence at home due to ill health, judge to review in 90 days</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/25/brazil-court-grants-temporary-house-arrest-for-jailed-bolsonaro_6751791_4.html'>Brazil court 